Now I can see clearly. Looking at lines 705-706 of static_inst.cc:```cpp
if (((el == EL0 && cpacr.fpen != 0x3) ||
    (el == EL1 && !(cpacr.fpen & 0x1))) &&
    !ELIsInHost(tc, el))
    return advSIMDFPAccessTrap64(EL1);
```

The condition checks `cpacr.fpen` not `cpacr.cp10`! Let me look at how CPACR is accessed in the code. The code in process.cc uses `cpacr.cp10` but the actual check uses `cpacr.fpen`.

In our process.cc:
```cpp
CPACR cpacr = tc->readMiscReg(MISCREG_CPACR_EL1);
cpacr.cp10 = 0x3;
cpacr.cp11 = 0x3;
cpacr.zen = 0x3;
tc->setMiscReg(MISCREG_CPACR_EL1, cpacr);
```

But the check is:
```cpp
if (((el == EL0 && cpacr.fpen != 0x3) ||    (el == EL1 && !(cpacr.fpen & 0x1))) &&    !ELIsInHost(tc, el))
    return advSIMDFPAccessTrap64(EL1);
```

So we need to set `fpen` not `cp10`! The CPACR_EL1 register has:
- cp10, cp11: for AArch32 (legacy)
- fpen: for AArch64 (fp and neon enable) - bit 0 and 1

In AArch64, we need to set `fpen` field!

Let me verify this by checking the misc register definition.

